# Keep GUIDE.md current

`GUIDE.md` in the project root is the owner's map of the program: diagrams of
how the phone app, server, and website fit together, plus a one-line
description of every file. It is hand-written, so it only stays true if every
change that touches structure also touches the guide. Do that in the same
task, before finishing. Do not leave it as a suggestion.

## When to update

| You did this | Update this in GUIDE.md |
|--------------|-------------------------|
| Added, renamed, moved, or deleted a file in `lib/`, `server/`, `website/`, or `test/` | Section 7 "File map": add, rename, or remove its line |
| Added a screen, provider, or service in the app | Section 2 diagram: add the node and its arrows |
| Added or changed a server route (`/v1/...`) or a page URL | Section 1 and Section 6 diagrams |
| Changed how sync, merge, or sharing works | Section 3, 4, or 5 (sequence / flowchart + rule table) |
| Introduced a new word that appears in several files (a new model, store, or concept) | Section 8 "Words used in the code" |
| Changed how to run or test something | Section 9 |

Small edits inside an existing file (bug fix, wording, styling) do not need a
guide change unless the file's one-line description is no longer true.

## How to write the line

One line per file, plain language, written for a person who does not code
every day. Say what the file is *for*, not what it imports.

```
# ❌ BAD
plan_card.dart   StatelessWidget that renders a WorkoutPlan

# ✅ GOOD
plan_card.dart   One plan in the Plan Library list
```

Keep the existing order inside each folder block and match the column
alignment of neighbouring lines.

## Diagrams

Diagrams are Mermaid. Keep them at folder / big-file level; do not add every
helper. Avoid `;` inside sequence-diagram text (it splits statements) and use
`<br/>` for line breaks in labels. If you add a diagram, it must parse.

## Finishing

Before you end a task that added or removed files, re-read Section 7 and
confirm each new path is listed and each removed path is gone.
